      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH05\",\n      \"title\": \"局限性、异质性与转化研究方向\",\n      \"purpose\": \"综合评估当前证据的成熟度，明确方法学挑战、机制不确定性及临床转化障碍，为未来研究优先级提供依据。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖 III 期 RCT 缺失的现状确认、观察性与干预性证据的等级差异、微生物组研究的方法学异质性（测序、队列、地理）、代谢物量化的技术缺口、干预策略（FMT、益生菌）的安全性与标准化挑战，以及宿主混杂因素（饮食、药物、共病）的控制需求。排除将临床前机制直接外推为临床事实的过度断言。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0020\",\n        \"P0024\",\n        \"P0048\",\n        \"P0051\",\n        \"P0099\",\n        \"P0184\",\n        \"P0199\",\n        \"P0302\",\n        \"P0315\",\n        \"P0340\",\n        \"P0344\",\n        \"P0371\",\n        \"P0373\",\n        \"P0378\",\n        \"P0404\",\n        \"P0405\",\n        \"P0410\",\n        \"P0411\",\n        \"P0421\",\n        \"P0426\",\n        \"P0429\",\n        \"P0440\",\n        \"P0441\",\n        \"P0453\",\n        \"P0461\",\n        \"P0465\",\n        \"P0467\",\n        \"P0480\",\n        \"P0488\",\n        \"P0491\",\n        \"P0492\",\n        \"P0508\",\n        \"P0519\",\n        \"P0527\",\n        \"P0528\",\n        \"P0531\",\n        \"P0538\",\n        \"P0551\",\n        \"P0558\",\n        \"P0579\",\n        \"P0580\",\n        \"P0581\"\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"证据天花板：III 期 RCT 缺失与证据等级\",\n          \"argument\": \"确认截至 2025 年末无完成的大型 III 期 RCT 证实微生物干预的生存获益，当前证据主要依赖 I/II 期试验及观察性数据，需明确区分关联与因果。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 90,\n            \"sha256\": \"1d14e1ea708998adcf63b173b6be431def1a020c5550d53631e3a1d33b424e1b\"\n          },\n          \"details\": \"引用文献计量学分析（P0001, P0501）及系统综述（P0026, P0355）确认领域现状。对比 FMT-LUMINate 等 II 期试验的高 ORR 与 MITRIC 的阴性结果（P0578, P0583），说明早期试验的变异性。强调观察性抗生素研究（P0575, P0576）的混杂局限。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"方法学异质性：从分类学到功能组的范式转变\",\n          \"argument\": \"不同研究间微生物标志物重复性低，受测序技术、队列特征及地理饮食因素影响，需从物种水平转向功能通路及多组学整合。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 81,\n            \"sha256\": \"cc3250127de2a38a24a64dfd3194eb1466c8a2bea3e9f3738e5b6073249c4dcd\"\n          },\n          \"details\": \"利用跨队列分析（P0478, P0565）展示标志物不一致性。引入“功能趋同”假说（P0364, P0496）解释物种差异。讨论人群特异性（如波兰队列 P0545）及多界微生物（P0393）的重要性。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"机制不确定性：代谢物量化与因果链条缺口\",\n          \"argument\": \"代谢物（如肌苷、SCFA）的绝对浓度数据缺失，多数机制基于小鼠模型，人体内因果路径及剂量效应尚不明确。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 81,\n            \"sha256\": \"90db55388d5dced31c6d6b5ba3586ebdb0e4b702979514fbb86b59550a74b876\"\n          },\n          \"details\": \"指出肌苷等代谢物缺乏人体 TME 绝对浓度数据（P0588, P0591）。强调代谢物效应的双向性及情境依赖性（P0326, P0476, P0559）。区分外源补充与内源产生的差异（P0588）。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"临床转化障碍：安全性、标准化与监管挑战\",\n          \"argument\": \"FMT 及活体生物药面临供体筛选、定植持久性、严重 irAEs 风险及监管指南（FDA/EMA）不完善的挑战。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 81,\n            \"sha256\": \"eca23628865c068be31558947aa2bb6eb52803f409608e4238a42db46c6645d3\"\n          },\n          \"details\": \"分析 FMT 试验中的毒性信号（如双免疫治疗下结肠炎 P0589）。讨论供体特异性（P0178）及工程菌的监管状态（P0586）。对比不同干预策略（益生菌 vs FMT）的证据等级（P0387, P0546）。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"宿主与环境混杂：药物、饮食及生理状态\",\n          \"argument\": \"抗生素、PPI、饮食及宿主生理状态（年龄、共病）显著修饰微生物组 -ICI 关联，需在研究设计中严格控制。\",\n          \"sources\": {\n            \"redacted\": true,\n            \"original_bytes\": 81,\n            \"sha256\": \"9f0549d660c9c5815141c5a84e1d24e72bec4b98743517823fe20ae0b69475a8\"\n          },\n          \"details\": \"量化抗生素时机效应（P0575, P0576）。讨论 PPI 与化疗的交互作用（P0537）。强调饮食纤维与商业益生菌的相反效应（P0454）。提及老龄化对菌群的影响（P0484）。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"本章作为综述的收尾，不重复前文机制细节，而是对全篇证据进行批判性综合。从 CH04 的干预可行性自然过渡到转化瓶颈，明确指出当前证据不足以支持常规临床应用，需通过标准化 III 期试验填补因果空白。结论将呼应 CH01 提出的证据天花板，形成闭环。\",\n      \"supplement_requests\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are there any completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials of microbiome interventions in ICI-treated solid tumour patients?\",\n          \"usable_content\": \"The supplied text explicitly states that as of late 2025, no completed Phase III randomized trials have confirmed a reproducible survival benefit of microbiome-based interventions in oncology. It identifies the current body of evidence as relying primarily on Phase I/II trials (e.g., FMT studies NCT03353402, NCT03341143; engineered bacteria trials NCT04167137, NCT03637803) and meta-analyses of these smaller datasets. The text details specific early-phase findings, such as FMT re-sensitizing ~40% of refractory melanoma patients to PD-1 blockade and engineered strains like SYNB1891 showing safety signals in Phase I, but consistently notes the absence of large-scale Phase III efficacy data (OS/PFS) required to fulfill the gap criteria.\",\n          \"conditions\": [],\n          \"limits\": [\n            \"Published primary outcome data from any completed Phase III RCTs of microbiome interventions (FMT, probiotics, consortia) in ICI-treated solid tumour patients.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        \"P0501\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0589\",\n        \"P0591\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 5 (CH05) of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nThe chapter title is \"局限性、异质性与转化研究方向\" (Limitations, Heterogeneity, and Translational Research Directions).\nThe purpose is to address evidence gaps, methodological challenges, and clarify research priorities.\nThe scope adjustment emphasizes that the lack of Phase III RCTs is a confirmed field limitation, not a retrieval failure. It also highlights the need to distinguish observational associations from causal mechanisms and the lack of absolute metabolite concentration data.\n\nI need to structure the chapter proposal with:\n1.  **Chapter ID & Title**: CH05, 局限性、异质性与转化研究方向.\n2.  **Purpose**: Synthesize limitations, heterogeneity sources, and future directions.\n3.  **Scope**: Focus on evidence gaps (Phase III RCTs, metabolite quantification), methodological challenges (standardization, confounding), and translational barriers (regulatory, safety).\n4.  **Substantive Threads**: Organize the content into logical themes (e.g., Evidence Ceiling, Methodological Heterogeneity, Mechanistic Uncertainty, Clinical Translation Barriers).\n5.  **Source Handles**: Select relevant sources from the provided `source_routing` that discuss limitations, heterogeneity, future directions, or lack of Phase III data.\n6.  **Excluded Sources**: Identify sources that are truly out of scope for this specific chapter (e.g., those focusing solely on specific bacterial mechanisms without discussing limitations/future directions, or those focused on non-solid tumors without relevant translational insights).\n7.  **Transition Logic**: How this chapter concludes the review.\n8.  **Supplement Requests**: Any specific data needs (though the prompt says limited supplementary search found no matching studies for Phase III, so I should reflect that).\n\nKey constraints from the prompt:\n-   Do not write a Q&A list.\n-   Do not assume a single research paradigm.\n-   Distinguish association vs. causation.\n-   Preserve source metadata (source_handle).\n-   Do not drop routed sources unless genuinely out of scope (name them in excluded_source_handles).\n-   Correct overclaims (e.g., Phase III RCT absence is confirmed).\n-   Use Chinese for the proposal content.\n-   Return JSON only.\n\nPlan for CH05:\n1.  **Evidence Ceiling**: Confirm the absence of Phase III RCTs (CorpusId:285298099, P0001, P0501). Discuss the reliance on Phase I/II and observational data (P0577, P0578, P0583).\n2.  **Methodological Heterogeneity**: Sequencing techniques, sample types (stool vs. tissue), geographic/dietary confounders (P0170, P0478, P0545).\n3.  **Mechanistic Uncertainty**: Metabolite quantification gaps (inosine, SCFAs absolute concentrations), species vs. function debate (P0364, P0588, P0592).\n4.  **Clinical Translation Barriers**: Regulatory challenges (FDA/EMA), safety (FMT toxicity, P0589), standardization of interventions (P0178, P0387).\n5.  **Future Priorities**: Standardized protocols, multi-omics integration, Phase III trial design (P0026, P0586).\n\nI need to check the `source_routing` for sources assigned to CH05 and ensure they are utilized or explicitly excluded if not fitting the specific argument of this chapter. Many sources are assigned to multiple chapters. I will select those that specifically contribute to the \"limitations/future directions\" argument.\n\nSources to include (assigned to CH05 and relevant):\nP0001 (Bibliometric, knowledge gaps), P0004 (PDAC limitations), P0005 (Narrative review, unclear mechanisms), P0007 (Observational limits), P0008 (Pediatric data gap), P0010 (AYA limits), P0011 (GI cancer specificity), P0012 (TKI comparison), P0013 (AI future), P0015 (Strain level limits), P0016 (Opioids confounding), P0018 (Prostate cancer evidence gap), P0019 (Tumor microbiome vs gut), P0020 (Psych analogy)